Composition is not a ban on inheritance. Use inheritance when:

- the relationship is a true, stable **is-a**, and the child can stand in for the parent everywhere (a `Circle` and a `Rectangle` are both `Shape`s with `area()`);
- you are implementing an **interface** or abstract class so that many types can be used the same way (each channel above could implement a `Channel` interface);
- a framework expects it (extending a test case class, an exception class such as `InsufficientBalance(Exception)`).

Avoid it when you only want to reuse code, when behaviours combine, or when the "kind" of an object can change over time. A useful rule of thumb: **inherit interfaces freely, inherit implementations carefully**.
